From: LibreELEC maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] openvfd: make probe failure and platform teardown safe

Initialize the controller before publishing interfaces and unwind allocation,
GPIO, LED/sysfs and misc registration failures. Keep the module mutex alive
until the reboot notifier and platform driver are gone. Serialize shutdown
and clear singleton state on remove so a later bind initializes hardware.

An open misc file may survive unbind: retain its device allocation until the
last close and reject operations once detached. Use a sleepable LED callback
and grouped attributes so registration errors cannot leave partial sysfs.
Preserve the DT profile, userspace ABI and normal upstream display behavior.

diff --git a/driver/openvfd_drv.c b/driver/openvfd_drv.c
index 61f5e93..7a7f3ce 100644
--- a/driver/openvfd_drv.c
+++ b/driver/openvfd_drv.c
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
